  "implementation": [
    "Six root provider kinds. New gateway and Bedrock kinds require system-v1 before generation creation; ordinary provider CAS, immutable publication, stop/restart and recovery remain in the existing transaction.",
    "Gateway exposes HTTPS Responses/authorization/token URLs, public client ID, cookie delivery and optional loopback port only. New/changed targets require explicit credential-routing confirmation. Complete requirements replace user provider auth/header definitions; native owns ChatGPT and OAuth tokens separately.",
    "Bedrock uses native amazon-bedrock-runtime or amazon-bedrock with commercial region and fixed regional endpoint. A fixed native-UID token command outranks cached native AWS credentials; no browser command, profile, credential-process or arbitrary endpoint is accepted.",
    "The token-only verb is absent from control sudo authorization. Managed token bytes remain in root settings and native-group-readable environment delivery, outside TOML and argv. Switching kinds removes AWS environment fields; region/kind changes require a fresh token.",
    "Root catalog refresh returns source:native for these kinds; it performs no gateway or AWS discovery. Runtime search is disabled; Mantle permits disabled/cached. Native SDK config/credential paths are fixed to /dev/null and metadata lookup is disabled.",
    "Existing host-policy conflict/drift checks and separate host-namespace config-check are unchanged. Provider UI, explicitGatewayOauth initialization and diagnostic secret redaction were integrated by the parent/runtime agents."
  ],
